      {
        "id": 249353,
        "name": "angramainyu",
        "username": "angramainyu",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/a/d78d45/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2022-11-18T17:14:47.887Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Irrevenant\" data-post=\"6\" data-topic=\"29738\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/i/e0b2c6/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Irrevenant:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I’m suggesting the creator make the site do that automatically by default when it generates a new character.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>The counter-argument is that someone just wanting to bookmark or link to the page in general (or non-specific seed) now has to edit their link, so it becomes a usability hurdle for others. It also means that if you hit “refresh” you don’t get a new seed. The html-rich page solves this by have the button link that modifies the URL, but since the bland page is, well, bland, it can’t.  Seems like a conscious design and usability choice.</p>\n<p>If the creator wanted to add that option, I’d suggest sticking a parameter like “s/” in the URL and have that trigger the behaviour.</p>\n<p>You could always write a grease-monkey script or something that does that (just add the seed to the URL automatically) for you if you use that page that way extensively.</p>",
        "post_number": 7,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2022-11-18T17:20:45.545Z",
